 <iati-activity default-currency="EUR" hierarchy="2" humanitarian="0" iati-activities:version="2.02" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-40409352-PRJ13-152-0010</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Collaboration NL Universities / (Research) Institutions water and environment (2024-2026)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with our collaboration of the past years, this partnership is intended to have effect at two key levels: 1) Internally, to assist the IA and National Clusters to &#x2018;do things differently&#x2019; and 2) externally to work with NS partners supported by NLRC and IFRC to improve their humanitarian service delivery towards crisis affected people.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">N/A</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner national societies and communities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Specifically with the TU Delft, In order to reach this, as NLRC we aim to participate in two TUD course, Bachelor End Product (BEP) and Strategic Design Studio (SDS), in which student (groups) will work on defined challenges and problem statements, defined by NLRC colleagues. Depending on the outcome, NLRC idents to further explore the proposed ideas into its programming and that of its partner National Societies. This with the ultimate goal of NS being able to provide improved humanitarian services delivery towards crisis affected people.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We aim to continue and further strengthen our collaboration with several NL universities, including the Wageningen University and the Technical University of Delft. This in order to design improved or new products, services or approaches and to create knowledge within our water and environmental portfolio within the international humanitarian assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
